# --- Project safety rules. These are the reason this file matters. ----------
#
# This repository is the SERVICE PROVIDER'S. The customer's configuration data
# lives in their own environment, in the mirror repository on their GitLab — it
# must never reach this one. The rules below are the control that enforces that
# separation, not housekeeping: relaxing them moves customer data across an
# organisational boundary.
#
# Customer configurations are never committed here, not even as test data.
# Every test fixture is synthetic - see tests/conftest.py.
customer_configs/
*.cfg
*.txt
# ...but the broad *.txt rule above must not swallow the project's own files.
!requirements.txt

# HMAC redaction key. Its whole purpose is to live outside the repo: with the
# key, the redaction tokens can be recomputed from guessed passwords.
*.key
.hmac-key

# Database credentials. .env.example is the committed template; .env itself
# holds a real password and must never be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Pipeline output. Models are written to disk locally; committing them is a
# later stage and will target a separate mirror repository, not this one.
out/

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# --- Editors and operating systems -----------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
